<title>NETHERLANDS: Kleiterp named president of merged Dutch bourses.</title>
<headline>Kleiterp named president of merged Dutch bourses.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Amsterdam Stock Exchange (AEX) said on Friday that Han Kleiterp would be appointed president of the supervisory board of the to-be-merged AEX and European Options Exchange (EOE) in Amsterdam.</p>
<p>The AEX, the world's oldest bourse, earlier this month announced the merger in response to increasingly fierce foreign competition ahead of European Economic and Monetary Union.</p>
<p>Kleiterp retired in 1994 as chief executive of MeesPierson, the investment banking subsidiary of ABN AMRO NV.</p>
<p>He is also chairman of ABP, the world's second largest pension fund.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
